{"agent":"fleet-dx-p","data":{"by":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","evidence":{"chunk_findings":[{"chunk":1,"detail":"The config change puts a template placeholder into the gate command itself (`command = \"uv run pytest tests/ -q --timeout=420 -n {workers}\"`), but only `data[\"command\"]` is ever substituted. `operations.py` builds the payload from `show_full, full = full, gate.command if gate else \"\"` and passes `full` (i.e. the raw `gate.command`, now containing `{workers}`) into `_selection_data(...)`; that helper receives no config object, so it cannot substitute anything, and therefore `data[\"full_suite\"]` is still the literal string `uv run pytest tests/ -q --timeout=420 -n {workers}`. The line below only blanks it when `show_full` is false, so when the whole‑suite command is requested (`ddflow tests --full`, i.e. `show_full=True`, which the adjacent comment says is \"the merge queue's and the phase end's\" command) the emitted/consumed command carries `{workers}` verbatim. Demonstration: run `ddflow tests <item> --full`; `data[\"full_suite\"]` ends in `-n {workers}`, and any consumer that executes it (or even just uses it as the parity/evidence command) hands pytest `-n {workers}`, which pytest-xdist rejects as an invalid int, so the whole-suite run cannot start. The same `full` value is also reused for the \"full\" command shown in the gate evidence, so the placeholder can leak there too. The substitution needs to be applied to every command string built from `gate.command` (at minimum `data[\"full_suite\"]`/`full`), not only `data[\"command\"]`.","digest":"4eda17f6a406e4b5","location":"ddflow/api/operations.py:360 (`data[\"command\"], auto = WK.resolve(...)`)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/api/operations.py:360 (`data[\"command\"], auto = WK.resolve(...)`)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"`_TEST_FILE.search()` matches on any token, so option *values* that merely name a test file are counted as if they were selected tests. `shlex.split(\"... --ignore=tests/test_slow.py tests/\")` yields the single token `--ignore=tests/test_slow.py`, whose suffix `/test_slow.py` matches `(?:^|/)(?:test_[^/]*|[^/]*_test)\\.py$`, so `count_test_files` returns 1 even though the command selects a whole directory. `compute` then executes `n = min(n, files)` (line 72), so a command like `pytest -n {workers} --ignore=tests/test_slow.py tests/` gets `-n 1` on a quiet 192-core host that would otherwise compute dozens of workers. The same false positive hits `--deselect tests/test_a.py::test_x` (the `(?:::.*)?` suffix even makes node ids match) and any other flag whose value ends in `_test.py`/`test_*.py`; exclusions are not workload, and the cap should be derived from selected files only (or from counting .py tokens that are not attached to an option).","digest":"a169e8a90e832b3e","location":"ddflow/services/workers.py:83 (count_test_files)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"ddflow/services/workers.py:83 (count_test_files)"},{"chunk":3,"detail":"The load-unavailable fallback `n = min(hi, UNKNOWN_LOAD_WORKERS)` never applies the lower bound, so it can return fewer than `[ci].min_workers` and break the documented clamp. With `ci.min_workers = 24`, `ci.max_workers = 48`, and a `SignalSource` whose `sample()` has no `\"load\"` key, `load is None` takes this branch and returns `n = 16`, below the configured minimum (the memory branch is not reached either unless `free` is present). The fallback should be `max(lo, min(hi, UNKNOWN_LOAD_WORKERS))` to preserve the `[min, max]` invariant.","digest":"d28fdd52ad2ebf03","location":"ddflow/services/workers.py:56 (compute)","severity":"LOW","title":"ddflow/services/workers.py:56 (compute)"},{"chunk":4,"detail":"Every other test in this file pins the machine input through the `run()` helper (`cores=192`), but this one calls `WK.resolve(cmd, cfg(), source=src)` with no `cores` argument, and `cfg()` carries no `cores` field. `resolve` must therefore read the core count from the host itself, so the substituted count is a function of the machine running the suite. With `source = FakeSource({\"load\": 0.0, ...})`, `load_per_core.high = 0.75`, and `min_workers = 1`, a 2-core runner computes `floor(2 * 0.75 - 0.0) = 1`, so `resolve` returns `\"pytest -n 1 tests/test_a.py tests/test_b.py\"` (1 < the 2 selected files, so the file cap does not raise it back to 2), and the assertion `cmd == \"pytest -n 2 tests/test_a.py tests/test_b.py\"` fails. Since the feature is explicitly meant to adapt to small/busy machines, the worker count produced by `resolve` needs to be pinned by injecting cores (or by having `resolve` accept a cores argument), otherwise this test is non-hermetic and goes red on 1–2 vCPU runners/containers.","digest":"c27e87143a7581b4","location":"tests/test_auto_workers.py:47 (test_resolve_substitutes_every_form_and_logs_inputs)","severity":"MEDIUM","title":"tests/test_auto_workers.py:47 (test_resolve_substitutes_every_form_and_logs_inputs)"}],"chunks_total":4,"coverage":"4/4 chunk(s) reviewed","delta_rounds":0,"diff_chars":17644,"diff_sha":"ee07c454f1a8401053ce74c4db9081f55dccdebd5f3af24787921c7f5269f620","diff_source":"main..HEAD + tracked working-tree changes in [REDACTED:path]","diff_stat":{"deletions":0,"files":0,"insertions":0,"untracked":0},"elapsed_s":1095.6,"family":"deepseek","findings":4,"max_chunk_chars":5000,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash","output_digest":"977d880c36d61fba","output_file":".ddflow/local/reviews/DX-xdist-auto-workers.rubber_duck.lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash.20261018T155457Z-64fab2ed.jsonl","reason":"","review_kind":"full","reviewed":[1,2,3,4],"reviewed_head":"cfc56598a54d07a76cd15e0a1ddf6babb8624ec4","reviewer":"lan-deepseek-v4.1-flash","reviewer_digest":"d34b8af1b4a590b5","round":1,"rounds":1,"status":"REVIEWED","titles":["ddflow/api/operations.py:360 (`data[\"command\"], auto = WK.resolve(...)`)","ddflow/services/workers.py:83 (count_test_files)","ddflow/services/workers.py:56 (compute)","tests/test_auto_workers.py:47 (test_resolve_substitutes_every_form_and_logs_inputs)"],"tree_sha":"cfc56598a54d+clean","unreviewed":[],"waves":1},"gate":"rubber_duck","reason":"4 finding(s)"},"id":"e64502bd12417ed2229e3443c","kind":"gate.failed","lamport":81800,"schema":1,"subject":"DX-xdist-auto-workers","ts":"2026-10-18T16:13:13.181519Z"}
